From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dmitry Afonchenko <undermove1@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 27 Nov 2026 11:32:33 +0400
Subject: [PATCH] Meridian: the Boost editor as Arc's, pixel for pixel, Code a
 page of its own, the badge's stars
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Measured on the owner's Arc screenshots and recordings (2x, frame by
frame) and checked in headless Chrome against them:
- The card: 183 px, Arc's greys, radii (13/15/14/8/11), 40 px head with
  the grey ✕ disc, the name ▾ (a menu: Rename, on/off, Delete) and reset.
- The pad: Arc's rim sampled every 5° (and its grey rim with no colour),
  the field a 5 % veil of the rim with a dot every 4 px, 36/24 px knobs in
  Arc's colours (52 %/49 %, 30 %/16 %), the grey knobs where Arc puts them.
- Arc's 20 fonts in Arc's order (each cell matched against every face on
  the Mac), 12 px, the one in use on a 26 px disc.
- Tiles 38 px; under the pointer a shade darker at once, icons still
  (as on Arc's recording); Size on Arc's orange.
- Code: the card widens to 480 px and slides to «← Back», CSS | JS, the
  editor and a toolbar (eyedropper, hammer = apply).
- Improve a row like Zap and Code.
- The badge in the site controls: the boost's dark colour, a brush and
  three stars twinkling every 1.65 s (Arc's timings within a frame).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01SwxrQ2eLfJ2bv8cCoG2va1
